   216	| Job / blocking check | Actor trust and input | Token / environment / secrets | Network | Outputs / retention | Approval |
   217	| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
   218	| `release/candidate-identity` | Default-branch `workflow_run`; independently read run/ref metadata, exact default-branch-reachable candidate commit, tag/version, trusted workflow SHA and policy digest; no intake payload | `contents: read`, `actions: read`; no production environment; no secrets | GitHub repository/workflow metadata read only | Immutable candidate manifest, intake/run identity, tag/ref and workflow-provenance evidence; release-record/7y | None |
   219	| `release/revalidate` | Exact candidate manifest | `contents: read`; no production environment; no secrets | Same allowlists as credential-free CI | Fresh results for every active required check, with digests | None |
   220	| `release/review-gate` | Exact manifest plus complete active evidence index | `contents: read`; no production environment; no secrets | Deny | Machine verdict: promotable/non-promotable/unknown; release-record/7y | Recorded engineering/security/release approvals; human ratification remains `TASK-260717-2d308k` before publication |
   221	
   222	The candidate manifest records source commit, clean-state assertion, source and
   223	dependency locks, toolchain/SDK/runner images, protocol and relay manifests,
   224	marketing/build versions, expected artifact names, the trusted caller workflow
   225	SHA/policy digest, every reusable-workflow SHA/file digest, and every evidence
