   275	## 4. Required-check and branch-protection policy
   276	
   277	The protected default branch and merge queue require the following exact check
   278	names. A skipped, cancelled, timed-out, neutral, stale, missing, or unknown
   279	result is non-success and blocks merge. Administrators and bots do not bypass
   280	the rule; emergency changes use the separately audited exception process and
   281	must restore all checks before release eligibility.
   282	
   283	1. `policy/github-actions`
   284	2. `policy/board-spec`
   285	3. `policy/version-release-metadata`
   286	4. `build/workspace-legacy`
   287	5. `test/core-protocol`
   288	6. `build/apple-credential-free`
   289	7. `build/relay-four-target`
   290	8. `security/supply-chain`
   291	9. `security/ci-threat-model`
   292	
   293	Checks are accepted only for the exact current pull-request head SHA. A base
   294	update, force-push, merge-queue synthetic commit, workflow-policy change, or
   295	dependency-lock change invalidates stale results. Branch protection must reject
   296	ambiguous duplicate check names from different workflows/apps. Release
   297	promotion additionally requires the three `release-prepare` checks and the
   298	applicable protected release receipts; PR checks alone never authorize release.
