   336	## 6. Artifact, provenance, retention, and network policy
   337	
   338	### 6.1 Required provenance envelope
   339	
   340	Every uploaded result contains a versioned manifest with: workflow/run/attempt,
   341	event and actor trust class, exact source and protected-base commits, dirty-state
   342	assertion, dependency lock digests, action SHAs, runner image, Xcode/SDK/Swift,
   343	Mise/Tuist, Go and scanner versions, relay/protocol manifests and versions,
   344	marketing/build versions, command inventory and exit status, artifact size and
   345	SHA-256, signing public identity/team/profile identifier and expiry where
   346	applicable, approval/environment receipts, and a redaction declaration. Private
   347	material, secret values, raw profiles, user-home paths, traffic, destinations,
   348	DNS names, cookies, and tokens are forbidden.
   349	
   350	Artifacts are uploaded under attempt-unique, candidate-digest-addressed names.
   351	Every downstream download verifies the expected manifest digest and each file
   352	digest before use. GitHub artifact IDs or filenames alone are insufficient.
   353	Release jobs rebuild from the immutable candidate or consume only protected
   354	staging receipts; they never promote artifacts produced by untrusted PR code.
   355	
   356	### 6.2 Retention classes
   357	
   358	| Class | Content | Retention | Access/deletion |
   359	| --- | --- | --- | --- |
   360	| `diagnostic` | Redacted failed-step logs with no reusable binary | 14 days | Repository readers; automatic deletion |
   361	| `verification` | PR/test/SARIF/policy reports | 90 days | Repository readers/security as scoped; automatic deletion |
   362	| `candidate` | Unsigned/rebuilt candidate bytes and intermediate manifests | 180 days or candidate rejection + 30 days, whichever is later | Release/security; digest-indexed deletion audit |
   363	| `release-record` | Published hashes, provenance, approvals, public signing/notary/feed receipts, SBOM/notices | 7 years | Append-only release/security evidence store; deletion requires recorded policy authority |
   364	| `incident-hold` | Minimum redacted subset named by an incident | Until explicit legal/security release | Restricted; hold and deletion events audited |
   365	
   366	Retention clocks and legal-hold applicability are policy-fill decisions for
   367	later owner ratification; they do not authorize storing secrets or personal
   368	traffic data.
   369	
   370	### 6.3 Network and cache rules
   371	
   372	- Deny network by default after bootstrap. Allow only exact GitHub endpoints,
   373	  checksum-pinned package/tool origins, advisory databases, Apple notarization,
   374	  GitHub publication, and the Relux update origin in the job that owns them.
   375	- Redirects, new hosts, mutable bootstrap responses, proxy injection, or TLS
   376	  failure fail closed. Network inventories are retained in sanitized metadata.
   377	- Fork PRs may restore only read-only caches keyed by trust class, OS image,
   378	  exact tool/dependency/source hashes, and cache schema. They never save to a
   379	  namespace restored by trusted/release jobs.
   380	- Cache contents are never authoritative. Checksums, manifests, generated drift,
   381	  linkage, and artifact inspection run on every hit. Poisoned or unreadable
   382	  caches are discarded and the job rebuilds; inability to rebuild is failure.
   383	
   384	## 7. Threat and failure-path contract
   385	
   386	| Scenario | Required prevention/detection | Fail-closed result and recovery owner |
   387	| --- | --- | --- |
   388	| Forked code | No environment, secret, write token, self-hosted runner, privileged reusable workflow, or trusted cache/artifact namespace | PR remains failing; `TASK-260715-2wjvlx` fixes policy, `TASK-260715-vg2of8` proves it |
   389	| Mutable action | Full-SHA policy rejects tag/branch/range before action execution | `policy/github-actions` fails; security reviews replacement SHA |
   390	| Cache poisoning | Trust-separated keys; content verification after restore; release ignores PR caches | Discard/rebuild; verification failure blocks the owning build check |
   391	| Artifact substitution | Candidate manifest and per-file digests verified at each transfer; untrusted artifacts never promote | Consumer fails before processing; evidence owner records attempted digest mismatch |
   392	| Tag/workflow spoofing or race | Repository settings keep tag tokens read-only; production secrets exist only in default-branch-restricted environments; tag workflow is intake only; default-branch `workflow_run` independently resolves run/ref/ancestry; trusted caller and reusable workflow SHA/digests are fixed | Missing/ambiguous metadata, mutated/missing intake, non-default workflow provenance, candidate/tag-ref workflow code, or digest mismatch makes `release/candidate-identity` unknown/failing before environment access |
   393	| Rerun | Original candidate manifest/digests and policy revision remain fixed; attempt number is new | Changed identity creates a new candidate, not a rerun; old attempt stays non-promotable |
   394	| Cancellation/timeout/runner loss | Bounded jobs, `always()` evidence finalizer that cannot override failure, no feed publication before all receipts | Cancelled/unknown, never success; revoke temporary material and resume from last immutable receipt |
   395	| Concurrent releases | One production concurrency group, no cancel-in-progress, monotonic version reservation | Later candidate waits; conflicting version is rejected, never overwritten |
   396	| Compromised low-privilege credential | Job-specific endpoint/scope; cannot sign, alter candidate, approve environment, or delete evidence | Stop affected job, revoke/rotate, mark candidate non-promotable, security owns incident disposition |
   397	| Missing/expired credential | Preflight proves availability without printing material | Required credentialed job fails; it is never `skipped-as-pass` |
   398	| Partial publication | Versioned assets first, remote digest/header checks, signed feed atomically last | Feed withheld; exact receipts determine safe resume or withdrawal |
   399	| Scanner/advisory outage | Distinguish no findings from unavailable database/service | `unknown` blocks `security/supply-chain`; security owner decides only through audited exception |
   400	| Evidence/log upload failure | Gate result and evidence persistence are both required | Owning check fails even when build/tests passed |
   401	
   402	No workflow may convert failure into success with `continue-on-error`, blanket
   403	retry, fallback credentials, alternate unsigned feed/download, stale evidence,
   404	or a summary-only aggregator. Matrix aggregation reports every child result and
   405	fails unless all required children succeeded.
   406	
   407	## 8. Negative evidence obligations
   408	
   409	This task ships documentation, not enforcement code. The referenced
   410	`references/negative-evidence.md` was not present in the repository or installed
   411	skill trees during authoring, so its contents are `unknown`, not inferred.
   412	Downstream implementations still must add tests that narrow and prove each
   413	production call site:
   414	
   415	| Production call site | Minimum rejecting fixtures |
   416	| --- | --- |
   417	| `policy/github-actions` / `TASK-260715-2wjvlx` | write permission, protected environment on PR, mutable action, privileged runner, unsafe cache namespace, missing timeout, duplicate check name |
   418	| `policy/board-spec` / `TASK-260715-2hef52` | production-wrapper fixture with invalid hierarchy/status that proves reported issues cannot exit 0; missing/malformed/unreadable validator JSON; missing resource; broken ID/link; dependency cycle; spec-format failure; tracked mutation |
   419	| `build/workspace-legacy` / `TASK-260715-3mk4hs` | target/scheme removal, generator/identifier drift, dirty generation, legacy regression |
   420	| `test/core-protocol` / `TASK-260715-1m3edc` | omitted suite/vector, malformed/oversized input regression, timeout, leak, retry-dependent flaky pass |
   421	| `build/apple-credential-free` / `TASK-260715-1uxx3i` | identity lookup, iOS scheme in macOS-only mode, identifier/embed/entitlement/link/version drift, signing claim from unsigned output |
   422	| `build/relay-four-target` / `TASK-260715-36gq4m` | missing/duplicate target, mutable fetch, target/identity/protocol/checksum mismatch, partial matrix |
   423	| `security/supply-chain` / `TASK-260715-38atsq` | private key/token/password, prohibited license, vulnerable lock, missing SBOM component/notice, over-broad or expired suppression |
   424	| `security/sarif-publish` / `TASK-260715-38atsq`, `TASK-260715-2wjvlx` | PR/fork invocation, unprotected source, missing environment approval, report/source digest mismatch, permission broader than `security-events: write`, non-GitHub upload endpoint |
   425	| `policy/version-release-metadata` / `TASK-260715-2759wy` | malformed/nonmonotonic/duplicate tag or build, dirty source, missing release-note section, incompatible protocol |
   426	| `release/request-intake`, `release/candidate-identity`, and `release/review-gate` / `TASK-260715-2ybl7y` | tag outside protected history whose tagged workflow deletes/forges the guard; non-default/selectable-ref dispatch attempt; intake artifact/cache/output offered as authority; missing/mismatched `github.workflow_sha` or policy digest; relative or candidate/tag-ref reusable workflow; stale check SHA; missing approval/evidence; duplicate version; cancellation; mixed receipts. Each fixture must prove rejection before candidate acceptance or protected-environment access |
   427	| Artifact/evidence consumers / `TASK-260715-82zzad` | digest substitution, missing file, tamper, redaction failure, expired evidence, artifact-ID/name collision |
   428	| `release/relay-stage` / `TASK-260715-2ybl7y`, `TASK-260715-pa6evr` | direct/unapproved invocation, wrong candidate or digest, substituted bytes, missing environment approval, compromised staging credential attempting sign/publish/delete, concurrent version collision |
   429	| `release/macos-sign-notarize` / `TASK-260715-3gkwn0`, `TASK-260715-3sk5cd`, `TASK-260715-387eof` | missing/expired/wrong-scope credential, approval bypass, identity/profile/entitlement mismatch, notarization reject/timeout/unknown, post-notary byte mutation, concurrent candidate |
   430	| `release/macos-sparkle-sign` / `TASK-260717-ziprhs` and macOS update pipeline owner | wrong candidate/DMG digest, missing two-custodian approval, key unavailable/compromised, signature verification failure, Developer ID and EdDSA rotation in one update |
   431	| `release/macos-publish-assets` / `TASK-260715-1njthi` | approval bypass, wrong digest/version, duplicate or mutable asset, partial upload, compromised token attempting signing/feed/evidence deletion, concurrent publication |
   432	| `release/macos-publish-feed` / macOS update pipeline and release owners | feed-before-assets, missing/failed remote digest/header/privacy probe, redirect or origin drift, partial/nonatomic feed write, wrong signature/channel/version, concurrent publication |
   433	
   434	Tests must assert the real nonzero/blocked result and the exact production
   435	validator or workflow job. Deleting a fixture or testing only an allow case is
   436	not evidence that the rejecting bound exists.
   437	
   438	## 9. Approval, disputes, and change control
   439	
   440	The autonomous draft is reviewed by an independent reviewer agent before the
   441	solution-architect handoff. Human security, release, and platform ratification
   442	is intentionally consolidated in `TASK-260717-2d308k`; its pending status does
   443	not block downstream implementation of this accepted draft, but publication
   444	cannot pass `release/review-gate` without its recorded verdict.
   445	
   446	No current trust decision is disputed. The exact retention durations,
   447	environment names, endpoint allowlists, and whether the separately protected
   448	trusted-branch SARIF publisher is enabled are policy-fill decisions because the
   449	source specs require those controls but do not fix their exact values. They were
   450	selected to produce a testable least-privilege contract after checking the
   451	task's explicit non-scope: they do not reinterpret A0, require Linux CI for the prototype,
   452	activate iOS, issue credentials, implement workflows, or make legal/App Review
   453	decisions. Human ratification may narrow them; any broadening requires a written
   454	threat-model delta, accountable security/release owner, negative fixture, and a
   455	fresh review.
   456	
   457	Any later dispute records: the exact row, current evidence, two or more viable
   458	options, security and release trade-offs, recommendation, accountable owner,
   459	and the decision deadline. Until resolved, the affected required check or
   460	release gate remains failing/unknown; unrelated credential-free work continues.
   461	
   462	Changes to workflow triggers, permissions, action pins, runner classes, cache or
   463	artifact trust, release environments, credential scope, publication order,
   464	retention, provenance schema, or required-check names require review of this
   465	contract and `.spec/threat-model.md` in the same change.
   466	
   467	## 10. External platform basis
   468	
   469	The trusted-entry design follows GitHub's documented execution model: a run
   470	uses workflow code from the event-associated SHA/ref; `workflow_dispatch` may
   471	select a branch or tag; `workflow_run` runs at the default branch and can cross
   472	into a privileged context; and full commit SHAs are the safest reusable-workflow
   473	reference. See [Workflows](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/concepts/workflows-and-actions/workflows),
   474	[events that trigger workflows](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/events-that-trigger-workflows#workflow_run),
   475	and [reuse workflows](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/reuse-automations/reuse-workflows).

