     1	# Validation strategy
     2	
     3	## Principles
     4	
     5	The riskiest assumptions are proven before broad UI work. Packet, SSH, relay,
     6	and lifecycle components are testable in `ReluxTunnelCore` or a macOS CLI
     7	harness; only Apple-specific packetFlow, entitlement, and lifecycle behavior
     8	require a signed provider on real hardware. Per ADR-024, macOS remains the
     9	active physical platform, but the current development Mac is build-only. All
    10	network-mutating macOS physical rows require the separate host gate
    11	`TASK-260819-25e1ys` and the fail-closed preflight in
    12	`scripts/physical-test-host-preflight.sh`. Physical-iPhone and jetsam rows are
    13	deferred with iOS and are recorded as named deferred gaps, never as passes.
    14	
    15	No validation on the build host may install a system extension or VPN app,
    16	persist a real VPN preference, call `startVPNTunnel`, activate a provider, or
    17	change routes or DNS. Build, compile, unit, harness, simulator, inspection, and
    18	unsigned-provider validation remain local-safe. `docs/build-host-safety.md` is
    19	the authoritative host-operation policy.
    20	
    21	Tests MUST record device/OS, source revision, dependency revisions, configuration,
    22	duration, traffic shape, loss/latency conditions, peak physical footprint,
    23	available-memory samples, channel/association counts, and drop/error counters.
