Verdict: **CHANGES REQUESTED**. CR revision 3 was not accepted; `TASK-260715-whtdsf` is routed to `to-dev`.

Blocking issue: the contract treats arbitrary tagged workflow code as externally constrained to read-only permissions, no network, and no artifact/cache authority. GitHub instead loads workflow YAML from the event ref, lets that YAML adjust `GITHUB_TOKEN` permissions, and gives standard hosted runners public Internet access by default. Repository “restricted permissions” are only defaults, not a hard ceiling. [GitHub workflow execution](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/concepts/workflows-and-actions/workflows), [permission calculation](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/workflow-syntax#how-permissions-are-calculated-for-a-workflow-job), [repository settings](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/enabling-features-for-your-repository/managing-github-actions-settings-for-a-repository#setting-the-permissions-of-the-github_token-for-your-repository), [runner networking](https://docs.github.com/en/enterprise-cloud@latest/actions/concepts/runners/private-networking#about-github-hosted-runners-networking).

